 17592186045498 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670781 1083 #uuid "ed9c8ce6-3232-550b-ba3e-f1ef8a153d5c" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670771 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670774 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670775 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670778 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670780 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1077 "selection" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670775 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670782 1079 #uuid "a46c3755-7eae-536c-bcdc-98a79dbadf22" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670767 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670769 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670773 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670776 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670781 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1077 "selection" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670781 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670783 1079 #uuid "aa63a6a8-e732-5c46-9e84-c078fc19694e" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670768 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670770 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670772 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670777 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670779 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1077 "selection" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670779 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670784 1079 #uuid "bc84df8d-7b1c-57bb-831f-bc0b1a17bb7a" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670785 1168 "generators/01/019074dd4d4f1c71c3480bf62963c6a730a8d2182fa68bb4ce67fb77736aa28c/generator.py" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670785 1169 #uuid "4fae9706-5008-5607-b0bb-3296938e831d" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670786 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670782 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670786 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670786 1071 "Assume $x>0$.\n\nExpress $3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)$ as a single logarithm." 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670786 1072 #uuid "41bba485-231e-5eaa-99c4-61446cde6137" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670786 1074 "Using the power rule for logarithms, rewrite the powered numerical term and evaluate the power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& 3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2^{3}\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(8\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, combine the factors with the same sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{3}\\left(8\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(8x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quotient rule for logarithms and simplifying the numerical factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{3}\\left(8x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{8x}{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& 3\\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)+\\log_{3}\\left(x\\right)-\\log_{3}\\left(4\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{3}\\left(2x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x>0$." 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670783 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670787 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670787 1071 "Assume $x,y,z>0$.\n\n$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right)=$" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670787 1072 #uuid "77c74a84-122e-5dd7-b170-e7f0507d8abe" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670787 1074 "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)+\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(ab\\right)$ — the product rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)-\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ — the quotient rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(c^{m}\\right)=m\\log_{n}\\left(c\\right)$ — the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)+\\log_{5}\\left(y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms (a square root is a power of one half), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)+\\log_{5}\\left(y^{2}\\right)-\\log_{5}\\left(z^{4}\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)+2\\log_{5}\\left(y\\right)-4\\log_{5}\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{2}}{z^{4}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)+2\\log_{5}\\left(y\\right)-4\\log_{5}\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$." 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670788 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670784 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670788 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670788 1071 "Assume $x,y,z>0$.\n\n$\\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right)=$" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670788 1072 #uuid "f3842e0a-970a-5ffe-87fc-38911ec62602" 13194139538567 17592186576411 true] [17592186670788 1074 "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)+\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(ab\\right)$ — the product rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(a\\right)-\\log_{n}\\left(b\\right)=\\log_{n}\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)$ — the quotient rule\n\n- $\\log_{n}\\left(c^{m}\\right)=m\\log_{n}\\left(c\\right)$ — the power rule\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{3}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}y^{3}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(y^{3}\\right)+\\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power rule for logarithms (a square root is a power of one half), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(y^{3}\\right)+\\log\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)-\\log\\left(z^{5}\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}y^{3}}{z^{5}}\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\log\\left(y\\right)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log\\left(x\\right)-5\\log\\left(z\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese identities hold for $x,y,z>0$." 13194139538567 17592186576411 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-052d61ab-849c-5821-a4c8-7b7df8edf4c1" 